  "units": [
    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Allows wrapped [references] and [boxes] to dangle.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            84,
            138
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            139,
            142
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " <section class=\"warning\">",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            143,
            172
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This type is not properly implemented yet, and the documentation below is thus not accurate.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            173,
            269
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " </section>",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            270,
            284
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            285,
            288
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " That is, if a reference (or a `Box`) is wrapped in `MaybeDangling` (including when in a",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            289,
            380
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " (nested) field of a compound type wrapped in `MaybeDangling`), it does not have to follow",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            381,
            474
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " pointer aliasing rules or be dereferenceable.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            475,
            524
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            525,
            528
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This can be useful when the value can become dangling while the function holding it is still",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            529,
            625
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " executing (particularly in concurrent code). As a somewhat absurd example, consider this code:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            626,
            724
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            725,
            728
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```rust,no_run",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            729,
            747
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " #![feature(box_as_ptr)]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            748,
            775
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # use std::alloc::{dealloc, Layout};",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            776,
            816
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # use std::mem;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            817,
            836
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            837,
            840
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let mut boxed = Box::new(0_u32);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            841,
            877
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let ptr = Box::as_mut_ptr(&mut boxed);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            878,
            920
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            921,
            924
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " // Safety: the pointer comes from a box and thus was allocated before; `box` is not used afterwards",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            925,
            1028
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " unsafe { dealloc(ptr.cast(), Layout::new::<u32>()) };",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1029,
            1086
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1087,
            1090
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " mem::forget(boxed); // <-- this is UB!",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1091,
            1133
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1134,
            1141
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1142,
            1145
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Even though the `Box`'s destructor is not run (and thus we don't have a double free bug), this",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1146,
            1244
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " code is still UB. This is because when moving `boxed` into `forget`, its validity invariants",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1245,
            1341
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " are asserted, causing UB since the `Box` is dangling. The safety comment is as such wrong, as",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1342,
            1439
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " moving the `boxed` variable as part of the `forget` call *is* a use.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1440,
            1512
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1513,
            1516
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " To fix this we could use `MaybeDangling`:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1517,
            1562
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1563,
            1566
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```rust,no_run",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1637,
            1655
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " #![feature(maybe_dangling, box_as_ptr)]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1656,
            1699
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # use std::alloc::{dealloc, Layout};",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1700,
            1740
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # use std::mem::{self, MaybeDangling};",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1741,
            1783
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1784,
            1787
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let mut boxed = MaybeDangling::new(Box::new(0_u32));",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1788,
            1844
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let ptr = Box::as_mut_ptr(boxed.as_mut());",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1845,
            1891
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1892,
            1895
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " // Safety: the pointer comes from a box and thus was allocated before; `box` is not used afterwards",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1896,
            1999
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " unsafe { dealloc(ptr.cast(), Layout::new::<u32>()) };",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2000,
            2057
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2058,
            2061
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " mem::forget(boxed); // <-- this is OK!",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2062,
            2104
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2105,
            2112
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2113,
            2116
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Note that the bit pattern must still be valid for the wrapped type. That is, [references]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2117,
            2210
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " (and [boxes]) still must be aligned and non-null.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2211,
            2264
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2265,
            2268
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Additionally note that safe code can still assume that the inner value in a `MaybeDangling` is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2269,
            2367
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " **not** dangling -- functions like [`as_ref`] and [`into_inner`] are safe. It is not sound to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2368,
            2465
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " return a dangling reference in a `MaybeDangling` to safe code. However, it *is* sound",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2466,
            2555
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " to hold such values internally inside your code -- and there's no way to do that without",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2556,
            2648
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " this type. Note that other types can use this type and thus get the same effect; in particular,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2649,
            2748
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`ManuallyDrop`] will use `MaybeDangling`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2749,
            2795
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2796,
            2799
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Note that `MaybeDangling` doesn't prevent drops from being run, which can lead to UB if the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2800,
            2895
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " drop observes a dangling value. If you need to prevent drops from being run use [`ManuallyDrop`]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2896,
            2996
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " instead.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2997,
            3009
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3010,
            3013
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [references]: prim@reference",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3014,
            3046
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [boxes]: ../../std/boxed/struct.Box.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3047,
            3091
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`into_inner`]: MaybeDangling::into_inner",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3092,
